<title>HONG KONG: Taipei toppled as top Hong Kong air export market.</title>
<headline>Taipei toppled as top Hong Kong air export market.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taipei remained Hong Kong's leading trading partner for air cargo imports despite a sharp fall in tonnages but Tokyo Narita replaced the Taiwanese capital as the leading export destination in February, new statistics from Hong Kong's Civil Aviation Department show.</p>
<p>The amount of air imports from the Thai capital Bangkok continued to make a strong showing although more than 1,200 tonnes down on January.</p>
<p>Exports from the major destinations all showed a marked decrease when the Hong Kong market traditionally comes to a virtual standstill for the Chinese New Year holiday. Frankfurt remained the leading European airport of entry for Hong Kong goods followed by Paris Charles de Gaulle and London Heathrow.</p>
